            <!-- Moved out from inside `.editor-wrapper` to be a direct child of
                 `.split-panes-wrapper` instead (sibling of `.editor-wrapper`/`.terminal-wrapper`).
                 The mobile compiler/output tab toggle (`setSplitMode()` in client.js) shows one of
                 those two panes at a time via `display: none` on the other - since a `display: none`
                 ancestor hides descendants no matter their own `position` (fixed doesn't exempt an
                 element from an ancestor's `display: none`, it only takes the element out of normal
                 flow), nesting this group inside `.editor-wrapper` meant it vanished along with the
                 editor whenever the output tab was active. `.split-panes-wrapper` itself is never
                 hidden by the tab toggle, so this group now stays visible on both tabs. Staying a
                 descendant of `.split-panes-wrapper` (rather than moving further up, e.g. to
                 `.editor-workspace-wrapper`) also keeps the `.split-panes-wrapper.visualizing ...`
                 rules in playground.css (hiding `.mobile-run-button` / showing
                 `.mobile-visualize-controls-root` while visualizing) matching unchanged. -->
            <!-- React portal target for Visualize step controls, mobile-sized copy of
                 .visualize-controls-root (the desktop top-bar one) - same underlying
                 VisualizerControls instance's UI, portaled to two places at once, each
                 shown/hidden independently by CSS media query rather than duplicating any
                 component logic. Deliberately a SEPARATE `position: fixed` element from
                 `.mobile-float-actions` below (not a flex child of it) so it can be
                 horizontally centered on its own, independent of the Run/Visualize buttons'
                 right-anchored position - easier to see/reach mid-trace than tucked into the
                 corner group. -->
